          "changeMeaning": "Initial setup showing the central atom and the reference panel for Lewis structures.",
          "narration": "Welcome to the VSEPR theory lab. We explore how electron pairs around a central atom arrange themselves to minimize repulsion. Look at the water molecule; we start with a flat Lewis structure and use these principles to predict its 3D shape."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip1",
