          "changeMeaning": "Demonstrate the shift from methane to ammonia as a hydrogen atom is replaced by a lone pair.",
          "narration": "Now consider the distinction between electron-domain geometry and molecular geometry. In methane, all four domains are bonds. Replacing one with a lone pair makes the molecular shape trigonal pyramidal, even though the electron geometry remains tetrahedral."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip3",
